const P_CLOCK = "The town clock had stopped the night before the Harvest Festival. Nia, the clockmaker's apprentice, promised the mayor she would fix it by sunrise. First, she listened to the silent gears. Next, she drew every gear in her notebook and tested them one at a time. The wind rattled the tower windows as if it were laughing at her, but Nia kept working. At dawn, the clock coughed, groaned, and finally chimed. The whole town cheered.";
const P_RIVER = "The river grumbled all morning. It tossed branches like toys and whispered secrets to the reeds. Kai needed to cross it to bring his grandmother her medicine. He did not rush. He watched the water, found the shallow rocks, and tied a rope to an old oak tree. The oak tree held on tightly, like a strong friend. Step by careful step, Kai crossed safely.";
const P_LANTERN = "The Lantern Path: During a storm, the lighthouse lamp broke. Mei asked every neighbor to bring a lantern to the cliff path. Together they lined up the lights so the fishing boats could find the harbor. The wind howled and tugged at their coats, but the lanterns held steady. Mei's father made it home safely.";
const P_TOMAS = "Tomás and the River Bridge: A flood washed away the footbridge. Tomás's little sister needed medicine from across the river. He wanted to swim right away, but he remembered his abuela's advice to think first. He found the shallow rocks, tied a rope to a tree, and crossed slowly while the river snatched at his boots.";
const P_ABIGAIL = "The Bread Basket (1776): Abigail's mother baked bread for the soldiers every Tuesday. Today, a folded note was baked inside one loaf. Abigail's hands shook as she carried the basket past the guards at the bridge. \"Just bread for my aunt,\" she said, smiling even though her heart pounded like a drum. The guards waved her through. At the mill, a Patriot captain found the note and nodded. \"You've done your part,\" he said.";

